# STEP 2: SPACE INVADERS — PLAN.MD

```markdown
# Space Invaders — AAA Retro-Futurism Implementation Plan

## 1. CORE GAMEPLAY MECHANICS (Mathematical Model)

### Player Ship
- **Position**: `player.x ∈ [-BOUNDARY_X, BOUNDARY_X]`, fixed `y = PLAYER_Y`
- **Movement**: Velocity-based with acceleration/deceleration for smooth feel
  - `velocity *= FRICTION_PER_FRAME (0.85)`
  - `position += velocity * dt`
  - Clamp to boundaries with elastic bounce feedback
- **Shooting**: 
  - Cooldown timer: `SHOOT_COOLDOWN = 250ms`
  - Projectile spawned at `(player.x, player.y + OFFSET)` with `velocity_y = PROJECTILE_SPEED`

### Alien Grid System
- **Grid Layout**: 5 rows × 10 columns (classic), or scalable N×M
- **Movement Pattern**:
  ```javascript
  // Horizontal sweep
  grid.dx = DIRECTION * SPEED_BASE * difficultyMultiplier

  // Edge detection triggers drop + direction flip
  if (anyAlien.x < -BOUNDARY || anyAlien.x > BOUNDARY) {
    grid.dy -= DROP_DISTANCE;
    grid.dx *= -1;
    speedMultiplier += ACCELERATION_STEP; // Progressive difficulty
  }

  // Per-frame update
  alien.position.x += grid.dx * dt;
  alien.position.y += grid.dy * dt;
  ```

### Alien Types & Scoring
| Type | Row(s) | Points | Fire Chance | Speed Modifier |
|------|--------|--------|-------------|----------------|
| Squid (Top) | 0-1 | 30 | 0.8% | 1.0x |
| Crab (Mid) | 2-3 | 20 | 1.5% | 1.2x |
| Octopus (Bottom) | 4 | 10 | 2.0% | 1.5x |

### Bomb System (Alien Projectiles)
- Random alien selected per `BOMB_INTERVAL` frames
- Bomb spawns at `(alien.x, alien.y)` with `velocity_y = -BOMB_SPEED`
- Collision: AABB vs player hitbox → life lost + screen shake

### Boss UFO
- Spawns randomly every 15-25 seconds from left edge
- Travels across top at constant speed
- Destroying awards 150-300 points (randomized)
- Rare drop: power-up chance

### Win/Loss Conditions
- **Win**: All aliens destroyed → next wave with increased speed multiplier
- **Loss**: Player hit by bomb OR any alien reaches bottom threshold
- **Game Over**: Lives depleted to 0

---

## 2. MODERN AAA ENHANCEMENTS (18 Specific Upgrades)

### Visual Enhancements
| # | Enhancement | Three.js Implementation |
|---|-------------|------------------------|
| 1 | **Neon Emissive Glow** | `MeshStandardMaterial.emissive` + `UnrealBloomPass(threshold=0.2, strength=1.5, radius=0.4)` |
| 2 | **Procedural Alien Textures** | Canvas API: draw pixel-art patterns → `CanvasTexture` with linear filtering |
| 3 | **Animated Alien Squash/Stretch** | Per-frame scale modulation based on movement direction (squash on turn, stretch mid-move) |
| 4 | **Projectile Motion Trails** | `MotionTrailRenderer`: history buffer of positions → ribbon geometry with fading opacity |
| 5 | **Explosion Particle Bursts** | Pooled particles: sphere/box shapes, radial velocity, gravity, fade-out over lifetime |
| 6 | **Shockwave Rings on Death** | Expanding torus mesh with emissive material, scale + alpha decay over 0.3s |
| 7 | **Camera Shake (Trauma-Based)** | `camera.position += noiseVector * shakeIntensity`; intensity decays: `shake *= 0.92` per frame |
| 8 | **Hit-Stop Frame Freeze** | On impact: set `timeScale = 0` for 4 frames, then ramp back to 1.0 over 8 frames |
| 9 | **Floating Score Text (3D)** | Billboard sprites with CanvasTexture text, upward drift + fade animation |
| 10 | **Dynamic Background Stars** | Particle field with parallax scrolling based on player position |

### Gameplay Enhancements
| # | Enhancement | Implementation Details |
|---|-------------|------------------------|
| 11 | **Power-Up System** | Drop chance from UFO: SpreadShot (3 projectiles), Shield (absorb 1 hit), RapidFire (-50% cooldown) |
| 12 | **Combo Multiplier** | Consecutive kills without taking damage → multiplier up to 3x, visual counter on HUD |
| 13 | **Progressive Difficulty Scaling** | Wave N: `baseSpeed *= (1 + N * 0.15)`, alien fire rate increases with wave number |
| 14 | **Invulnerability Frames** | After taking damage: 2s blink invulnerability, hitbox disabled during off frames |
| 15 | **Screen-Space Threat Indicator** | Red vignette intensity scales with nearest bomb distance + alien proximity to bottom |

### Audio Enhancements (Web Audio API)
| # | Enhancement | Synthesis Method |
|---|-------------|------------------|
| 16 | **Procedural SFX Library** | Oscillators: sawtooth for shots, square waves for explosions, noise buffer for power-ups |
| 17 | **Dynamic Music Sequencer** | Bassline + arpeggio pattern that increases tempo with wave number (90 → 140 BPM) |
| 18 | **Audio Reactive VFX** | Particle emission rate modulated by music beat detection (low-frequency oscillator sync) |

---

## 3. GRAPHICS PIPELINE CONFIGURATION

### Renderer Setup
```javascript
const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ 
  antialias: false, // Post-processing handles this
  powerPreference: 'high-performance'
});
renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);
renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2)); // Cap at 2x for performance
```

### EffectComposer Stack (Render Order)
1. `RenderPass` — Base scene render
2. `UnrealBloomPass` — Neon glow effect
   ```javascript
   const bloom = new UnrealBloomPass(
     new THREE.Vector2(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight),
     1.5,    // strength (tuned for neon without washout)
     0.4,    // radius
     0.8     // threshold (higher = only brightest glow)
   );
   ```

### Material Strategy (MeshStandardMaterial Only)
```javascript
// Emissive neon material factory
function createNeonMaterial(color, emissiveIntensity = 1.0) {
  return new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({
    color: 0x111111,           // Dark base
    emissive: color,
    emissiveIntensity: emissiveIntensity,
    metalness: 0.3,
    roughness: 0.4,
    flatShading: true          // Retro low-poly look
  });
}

// Player ship material (cyan glow)
const playerMaterial = createNeonMaterial(0x00ffff, 1.2);

// Alien materials (type-specific colors)
const squidMaterial = createNeonMaterial(0xff00ff, 1.0);   // Magenta
const crabMaterial = createNeonMaterial(0x00ff00, 1.0);    // Green
const octopusMaterial = createNeonMaterial(0xffff00, 1.0); // Yellow
```

### Procedural Texture Generation (Canvas API)
```javascript
function generateAlienTexture(type) {
  const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
  canvas.width = 32; canvas.height = 32;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

  // Draw pixel-art alien pattern based on type
  // (binary sprite data converted to fillRect calls)

  const texture = new THREE.CanvasTexture(canvas);
  texture.magFilter = THREE.NearestFilter; // Retro crisp pixels
  texture.minFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;
  return texture;
}
```

### InstancedMesh for Alien Grid (Performance Critical)
```javascript
// Instead of 50 separate meshes, use ONE InstancedMesh per alien type
const squidGeometry = new THREE.BoxGeometry(1, 1, 0.2);
const squidInstancedMesh = new THREE.InstancedMesh(
  squidGeometry, 
  squidMaterial, 
  maxSquidCount // ~20 instances
);

// Update matrix per instance each frame based on grid position
const dummy = new THREE.Object3D();
for (let i = 0; i < activeSquidCount; i++) {
  const alien = squids[i];
  dummy.position.set(alien.x, alien.y, 0);
  dummy.updateMatrix();
  squidInstancedMesh.setMatrixAt(i, dummy.matrix);
}
squidInstancedMesh.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate = true;
```

---

## 4. VFX IMPLEMENTATION PRIORITY LOGIC

### Execution Order Per Frame (Critical Path)
```
1. Input Processing → Player Movement
2. Game Logic Update (aliens, projectiles, collisions)
3. Hit-Stop Check → If triggered, skip to step 8
4. Physics Integration (positions += velocity * dt)
5. VFX Updates:
   a. Particle Manager update (pool recycling, lifetime decay)
   b. Motion Trails buffer push/pop
   c. Shockwave scale + fade
   d. Floating Text drift + fade
6. Camera Shake Apply → camera.position offset
7. Render Pass
8. Hit-Stop Frame Counter Decrement
```

### Camera Shake System (Trauma-Based)
```javascript
// In shared/vfx/cameraShake.js
class CameraShake {
  constructor(camera) {
    this.camera = camera;
    this.intensity = 0;
    this.decayRate = 0.92;
    this.originalPosition = camera.position.clone();
  }

  addTrauma(impactVelocity) {
    // Scale shake by impact severity
    const baseShake = 0.3;
    const velocityScale = Math.min(impactVelocity / 10, 2);
    this.intensity += (baseShake + velocityScale) * 0.5;
  }

  update() {
    if (this.intensity <= 0.001) return;

    const angle = Math.random() * Math.PI * 2;
    const offsetX = Math.cos(angle) * this.intensity;
    const offsetY = Math.sin(angle) * this.intensity;

    this.camera.position.x = this.originalPosition.x + offsetX;
    this.camera.position.y = this.originalPosition.y + offsetY;

    this.intensity *= this.decayRate;
  }
}

// Usage: cameraShake.addTrauma(projectile.velocity.length()) on collision
```

### Hit-Stop / Frame Freeze System
```javascript
// In shared/vfx/hitStop.js
class HitStop {
  constructor() {
    this.framesRemaining = 0;
    this.totalFrames = 4; // Initial freeze duration
    this.rampDuration = 8; // Frames to ramp back to normal speed
  }

  trigger(impactSeverity) {
    // Severity scales freeze duration (1-8 frames)
    const baseFrames = Math.floor(impactSeverity * 3);
    this.framesRemaining = Math.min(baseFrames, 8);
    this.isRamping = false;
  }

  getTimeScale() {
    if (this.framesRemaining > 0) {
      this.framesRemaining--;
      return 0; // Complete freeze
    }

    if (this.rampFrame < this.rampDuration) {
      this.rampFrame++;
      return this.rampFrame / this.rampDuration; // Linear ramp
    }

    return 1.0;
  }
}

// In game loop: dt *= hitStop.getTimeScale();
```

### Particle Manager (Object Pool + 500 Hard Cap)
```javascript
// In shared/vfx/particles.js
class ParticleManager {
  constructor(maxParticles = 500) {
    this.maxParticles = maxParticles;
    this.particles = []; // Active particles
    this.pool = [];      // Recycled particles

    // Pre-allocate all particle objects
    for (let i = 0; i < maxParticles; i++) {
      this.pool.push(this.createParticleObject());
    }
  }

  createParticleObject() {
    return {
      mesh: new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material),
      position: new THREE.Vector3(),
      velocity: new THREE.Vector3(),
      lifetime: 0,
      maxLifetime: 0,
      active: false
    };
  }

  spawnBurst(position, count, color, velocitySpread) {
    // Respect hard cap
    const available = this.maxParticles - this.particles.length;
    const toSpawn = Math.min(count, available);

    for (let i = 0; i < toSpawn; i++) {
      let particle;

      if (this.pool.length > 0) {
        particle = this.pool.pop();
      } else {
        // Emergency: recycle oldest particle
        const oldest = this.particles.shift();
        this.recycleParticle(oldest);
        particle = oldest;
      }

      // Initialize burst parameters
      particle.position.copy(position);
      particle.velocity.set(
        (Math.random() - 0.5) * velocitySpread,
        (Math.random() - 0.5) * velocitySpread,
        (Math.random() - 0.5) * velocitySpread
      );
      particle.lifetime = particle.maxLifetime = Math.random() * 0.5 + 0.3;
      particle.active = true;

      this.particles.push(particle);
    }
  }

  update(dt) {
    for (let i = this.particles.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
      const p = this.particles[i];

      // Physics
      p.position.addScaledVector(p.velocity, dt);
      p.lifetime -= dt;

      // Fade out based on lifetime ratio
      const alpha = p.lifetime / p.maxLifetime;
      p.mesh.material.opacity = alpha;
      p.mesh.visible = alpha > 0.05;

      // Recycle when dead
      if (p.lifetime <= 0) {
        this.particles.splice(i, 1);
        this.recycleParticle(p);
      }
    }
  }

  recycleParticle(particle) {
    particle.active = false;
    particle.mesh.visible = false;
    particle.mesh.position.set(9999, 9999, 9999); // Off-screen
    this.pool.push(particle);
  }
}
```

### Motion Trails Implementation
```javascript
// In shared/vfx/motionTrails.js
class MotionTrailRenderer {
  constructor(maxSegments = 10) {
    this.maxSegments = maxSegments;
    this.trails = new Map(); // objectID → TrailData
  }

  add(object, color, thickness) {
    const id = object.id || Math.random();
    this.trails.set(id, {
      positions: [],           // History buffer (maxSegments Vector3s)
      color: new THREE.Color(color),
      thickness: thickness,
      geometry: null,          // Created on first update
      mesh: null
    });
  }

  update(object) {
    const trail = this.trails.get(object.id);
    if (!trail) return;

    // Push current position to history
    trail.positions.push(object.position.clone());

    // Maintain max length (FIFO)
    if (trail.positions.length > this.maxSegments) {
      trail.positions.shift();
    }

    // Update ribbon geometry
    if (trail.positions.length >= 2) {
      this.updateTrailGeometry(trail);
    }
  }

  updateTrailGeometry(trail) {
    // Create strip of quads along path
    const positions = [];
    const colors = [];

    for (let i = 0; i < trail.positions.length - 1; i++) {
      const t = i / trail.positions.length; // Alpha fade from tail to head
      const p1 = trail.positions[i];
      const p2 = trail.positions[i + 1];

      // Generate quad vertices perpendicular to motion direction
      const dir = new THREE.Vector3().subVectors(p2, p1).normalize();
      const right = new THREE.Vector3(-dir.z, 0, dir.x); // Perpendicular in XZ plane

      const halfWidth = trail.thickness * (t + 0.5) / 2;

      positions.push(
        p1.x - right.x * halfWidth, p1.y, p1.z - right.z * halfWidth,
        p1.x + right.x * halfWidth, p1.y, p1.z + right.z * halfWidth,
        p2.x + right.x * halfWidth, p2.y, p2.z + right.z * halfWidth,
        p2.x - right.x * halfWidth, p2.y, p2.z - right.z * halfWidth
      );

      // Color with alpha fade
      const alpha = t;
      colors.push(
        trail.color.r, trail.color.g, trail.color.b, alpha,
        trail.color.r, trail.color.g, trail.color.b, alpha,
        trail.color.r, trail.color.g, trail.color.b, alpha,
        trail.color.r, trail.color.g, trail.color.b, alpha
      );
    }

    // Update or create geometry
    if (!trail.geometry) {
      trail.geometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
      trail.geometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(positions, 3));
      trail.geometry.setAttribute('color', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(colors, 4));

      const material = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ 
        vertexColors: true, 
        transparent: true,
        side: THREE.DoubleSide,
        blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending
      });

      trail.mesh = new THREE.Mesh(trail.geometry, material);
      scene.add(trail.mesh);
    } else {
      trail.geometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(positions, 3));
      trail.geometry.setAttribute('color', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(colors, 4));
      trail.geometry.attributes.position.needsUpdate = true;
      trail.geometry.attributes.color.needsUpdate = true;
    }
  }
}
```

### Shockwave Rings
```javascript
// In shared/vfx/shockwave.js
class ShockwaveManager {
  constructor() {
    this.shockwaves = [];
    // Pre-create geometry/material for pooling
    this.geometry = new THREE.RingGeometry(0.1, 0.2, 32);
    this.baseMaterial = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({
      color: 0xffffff,
      transparent: true,
      opacity: 1,
      side: THREE.DoubleSide,
      blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending
    });
  }

  spawn(position, radiusMax = 3, duration = 0.3) {
    const material = this.baseMaterial.clone(); // Clone for independent opacity
    const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(this.geometry, material);

    mesh.position.copy(position);
    mesh.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2; // Lie flat on XZ plane

    this.shockwaves.push({
      mesh: mesh,
      radiusMax: radiusMax,
      duration: duration,
      startTime: performance.now() / 1000
    });

    scene.add(mesh);
  }

  update(dt) {
    const now = performance.now() / 1000;

    for (let i = this.shockwaves.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
      const sw = this.shockwaves[i];
      const age = now - sw.startTime;
      const t = age / sw.duration;

      if (t >= 1) {
        // Remove and dispose
        scene.remove(sw.mesh);
        sw.material.dispose();
        this.shockwaves.splice(i, 1);
        continue;
      }

      // Scale up + fade out
      const scale = t * sw.radiusMax / 0.2; // Normalize to initial geometry size
      sw.mesh.scale.set(scale, scale, 1);
      sw.mesh.material.opacity = (1 - t) * 0.8;
    }
  }
}
```

### Floating Score Text (3D Billboard + HTML Hybrid)
```javascript
// In shared/vfx/floatingText.js
class FloatingTextManager {
  constructor() {
    this.texts = [];
    this.canvasPool = []; // Reuse canvases for textures

    // HTML container for DOM-based floating text option
    this.htmlContainer = document.createElement('div');
    this.htmlContainer.className = 'floating-text-container';
    document.body.appendChild(this.htmlContainer);
  }

  spawn3D(position, text, color = '#00ff00', size = 24) {
    const canvas = this.getCanvas();
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,0)';
    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
    ctx.font = `bold ${size}px Arial`;
    ctx.fillStyle = color;
    ctx.textAlign = 'center';
    ctx.fillText(text, canvas.width / 2, canvas.height / 2 + size / 3);

    const texture = new THREE.CanvasTexture(canvas);
    const material = new THREE.SpriteMaterial({ 
      map: texture,
      transparent: true,
      depthWrite: false,
      blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending
    });

    const sprite = new THREE.Sprite(material);
    sprite.position.copy(position);
    sprite.scale.set(2, 1, 1); // Adjust for aspect ratio

    this.texts.push({
      mesh: sprite,
      lifetime: 1.5,
      velocityY: 0.5,
      htmlElement: null
    });

    scene.add(sprite);
  }

  spawnHTML(screenX, screenY, text, color = '#00ff00') {
    const el = document.createElement('div');
    el.className = 'floating-text';
    el.textContent = text;
    el.style.color = color;
    el.style.left = `${screenX}px`;
    el.style.top = `${screenY}px`;
    el.style.textShadow = `0 0 10px ${color}`;

    this.htmlContainer.appendChild(el);

    // Animate with CSS
    requestAnimationFrame(() => {
      el.animate([
        { opacity: 1, transform: 'translateY(0)' },
        { opacity: 0, transform: 'translateY(-30px)' }
      ], {
        duration: 1000,
        easing: 'ease-out'
      });
    });

    // Auto-remove after animation
    setTimeout(() => el.remove(), 1000);
  }

  update(dt) {
    for (let i = this.texts.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
      const ft = this.texts[i];

      ft.mesh.position.y += ft.velocityY * dt;
      ft.lifetime -= dt;
      ft.mesh.material.opacity = Math.max(0, ft.lifetime / 1.5);

      if (ft.lifetime <= 0) {
        scene.remove(ft.mesh);
        ft.material.dispose();
        this.texts.splice(i, 1);
      }
    }
  }

  getCanvas() {
    if (this.canvasPool.length > 0) {
      return this.canvasPool.pop();
    }
    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    canvas.width = 128;
    canvas.height = 64;
    return canvas;
  }
}
```

